  "description": "O'Connor Murphy Auctioneers are delighted to bring to the market 103 Oakleigh Wood, Dooradoyle. This spacious B rated, three-bedroom ground floor apartment with its own-door entrance offers bright, beautifully presented accommodation together with the rare benefit of a private, fully enclosed rear garden. Located in one of Limerick's most sought-after residential areas, this property is ideal for first-time buyers, those trading down, or anyone wishing to settle in a mature, convenient setting within walking distance of a host of amenities including the Crescent Shopping Centre, excellent schools and University Hospital Limerick.\n\nACCOMMODATION:\n\nThe property comprises of an entrance hallway, a bright open-plan living/dining room and kitchen, three bedrooms (main bedroom with ensuite and direct access to the rear garden) and a main bathroom.\n\n\nGROUND FLOOR:\n\nEntrance Hallway - Feature with tiled flooring with access to all principal rooms\nOpen Plan Kitchen/Living/Dining Room - Bright and spacious open-plan living and dining space with laminate wooden flooring, feature fireplace and feature coving. \nKitchen - Fitted wall and floor units with tiled flooring and tiled splashback. \nBedroom 1 - Rear facing double room with wooden flooring, built-in wardrobes and ensuite. Sliding patio door opening directly onto the private rear garden\nEnsuite - Shower room with shower, WC and WHB. tiled flooring\nBedroom 2 - Rear facing double room with laminate wooden flooring and built in wardrobes\nBedroom 3 - Front facing room with laminate wooden flooring and built in wardrobes\nMain Bathroom - Spacious Jack & Jill main bathroom comprising bath with an electric shower, WC and WHB\n\nEXTERIOR:\n\nFront - Own-door entrance with attractive brick and cut-stone facade, outdoor lighting and designated parking\nRear garden - Fully enclosed, private and rear garden with low-maintenance area. Accessed via sliding door from the main bedroom\n\n\nLOCATION:\n\n103 Oakleigh Wood is located in a mature, highly sought-after development just off the main Dooradoyle Road. The property is ideally positioned within walking distance of the Crescent Shopping Centre and several well-regarded primary and secondary schools, including Crescent College Comprehensive. The Rosedale Centre, with its convenience store, pharmacy and medical centre, is also within a short stroll. University Hospital Limerick and Raheen Business Park are both close by, making this an excellent base for those working in the area, while sports enthusiasts are well served by nearby clubs and leisure facilities. The location also offers easy access to the M20 Cork motorway, the M7 Dublin motorway, and the N18 Shannon/Galway Road.\n\n\n\n\nServices:\n\nGas Heating \nDouble Glazed Windows\nDesignated Parking Space\nManagement Fees Incurred\n\nAccommodation\n\n Note: \nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only. Property Reference :OMUR6817\nDIRECTIONS:\nV94 E138",
